      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2009-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Twenty percent less than \\(60\\) is \\(0.8 \\cdot 60 = 48.\\)\n\nOne-third more than \\(n\\) is \\(\\dfrac{4}{3}n,\\) so \\(\\dfrac{4}{3}n = 48\\) gives \\(n = 36.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
